{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/954011-home-brew-merit-off-hand-training","id":954011,"title":"Home-brew Merit: Off Hand Training","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-19T13:48:01-07:00","id":954011,"title":"Home-brew Merit: Off Hand Training","content":"<span style=\"color:#212121\"><span style=\"font-family:wf_segoe-ui_normal\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><b><u><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\">Off Hand Training <b><u><u><b><b><u><u><b><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\">(Weaponry or Firearms)</span></b></u></u></b></b></u></u></b> </span><u><b><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\">\u2022\u2022 or </span><b><u><u><b>\u2022\u2022</b></u></u></b><b><u><u><b><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\">\u2022 </span></b></u></u></b></b></u></u></b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#212121\"><span style=\"font-family:wf_segoe-ui_normal\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> N</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">ot everyone is born </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\">Ambidextrous, but</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\"> through dedicated training some may learn to fight as if they were. </span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Prerequisite:</b> Resolve \u2022\u2022\u2022, Composure \u2022\u2022\u2022, and Weaponry or Firearms \u2022\u2022</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Effect: </b><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">When this Merit is taken choose if it is for Firearms or Weaponry. You may take this Merit Twice, once for Firearms, and again for Weaponry.</span></span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The \u2022\u2022 version of this Merit allows you to reduce the off hand penalty for either Firearms or Weaponry to -1. The \u2022\u2022\u2022 Version of this Merit allows you to negate the off hand penalty for either Weaponry or Firearms.<br /> <br /> Notes:</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#212121\"><span style=\"font-family:wf_segoe-ui_normal\">Ambidextrous is </span></span><span style=\"color:#212121\"><span style=\"font-family:wf_segoe-ui_normal\">the better merit because it does more for less, but unlike Ambidextrous Off Hand Training can be learned after character creation so long as a character has the </span></span><span style=\"color:#212121\"><span style=\"font-family:wf_segoe-ui_normal\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">discipline</span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:wf_segoe-ui_normal, Segoe UI, Segoe WP, Tahoma, Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#212121\"> (Resolve 3 &amp; Composure 3) and skill (Firearms or Weaponry 2) to work towards overcoming the disadvantages of using their off hand. <br /> <br /> I designed this Merit with the idea of some Age of Sail Character Types potential running amok with a <span style=\"font-size:16px\">cutlass</span> in one hand and a pistol in the other, though I believe it could also be useful for wild west gunslingers, or any character who often finds themselves using their off-hand. It is not a dual wielding Merit, but simply a better at using your off hand in combat merit.</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4630-jmecha","name":"JMecha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T14:34:57-07:00","id":954044,"title":"","content":"That's really cool! I wonder if it should follow the model set by Fighting Finesse and work with a particular Specialty. Then you could take Off-Hand training in, for example, painting, or bowling, as well as handguns and swords.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T14:59:19-07:00","id":954052,"title":"","content":"I originally designed it to require Specializations just like you are pondering and I fully support your choice to house rule it that way if you do. I though feared there would be a riot of complaints at my table if the Merit required Characters to take Off Hand Training separately for all the various Specializations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4630-jmecha","name":"JMecha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T15:43:24-07:00","id":954069,"title":"","content":"At the two-dot level, wouldn't you be better off, cost-wise, taking a Skill Specialty (Off-hand) in Weaponry or Firearms to (effectively) reduce the penalty from -2 to -1?<br /> <br /> (And then Area of Expertise to negate the penalty. And then Interdisciplinary Specialty to completely replicate the effect of Ambidexterity, I guess.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T16:15:47-07:00","id":954087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JMecha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/954011-home-brew-merit-off-hand-training?p=954052#post954052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I originally designed it to require Specializations just like you are pondering and I fully support your choice to house rule it that way if you do. I though feared there would be a riot of complaints at my table if the Merit required Characters to take Off Hand Training separately for all the various Specializations.</div> </div> </div> </div>Makes sense. Either way, awesome concept, I think I'm going to use it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T16:56:03-07:00","id":954101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Five Eyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/954011-home-brew-merit-off-hand-training?p=954069#post954069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the two-dot level, wouldn't you be better off, cost-wise, taking a Skill Specialty (Off-hand) in Weaponry or Firearms to (effectively) reduce the penalty from -2 to -1?<br /> <br /> (And then Area of Expertise to negate the penalty. And then Interdisciplinary Specialty to completely replicate the effect of Ambidexterity, I guess.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Or<br /> You could take Off Hand Training to negate the Off Hand Penalty, and then take a Specialty in Off Hand combined with Area of Expertise to add bonus dice to your rolls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4630-jmecha","name":"JMecha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T17:00:20-07:00","id":954105,"title":"","content":"Charlaquin, <br /> <br /> Thank you for sharing your interest in the Merit. I am always happy to know I brought something of use to a table","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4630-jmecha","name":"JMecha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T20:26:42-07:00","id":954174,"title":"","content":"My mom used to get her left arm tied behind her back, and was taught to write with the right hand. What I'm getting at is that ambidexterity isn't restricted to character creation only nowadays, if you care to check it out (in 2e at least).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T20:53:40-07:00","id":954181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/954011-home-brew-merit-off-hand-training?p=954174#post954174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My mom used to get her left arm tied behind her back, and was taught to write with the right hand. What I'm getting at is that ambidexterity isn't restricted to character creation only nowadays, if you care to check it out (in 2e at least).</div> </div> </div> </div>...yes it is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chronicles of Darkness pg. 47</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ambidextrous (\u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> Effect: Your character does not suffer the -2 penalty for using his off hand in combat or to perform other actions. Available only at character creation</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T07:14:18-07:00","id":954361,"title":"","content":"Must've fixed it from God Machine Chronicles and Blood &amp; Smoke.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T09:07:12-07:00","id":954426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/954011-home-brew-merit-off-hand-training?p=954361#post954361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Must've fixed it from God Machine Chronicles and Blood &amp; Smoke.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The God-Machine Chronicle pg.164</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ambidextrous (\u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> Effect: Your character does not suffer the \u20132 penalty for<br /> using his off-hand in combat or to perform other actions. Available only at character creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>And Ambidexterous isn't in Blood &amp; Smoke","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T21:06:01-07:00","id":954792,"title":"","content":"Whatever. I could swear I saw an iteration of the merit without the CC clause.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}